>This list is considered private. That means that we have a number of
>rules about how you may use material you get from your membership to
>the list, and how you interact with the list. Your continued
>subscription indicates your acceptance of these rules.

Anonymous subscription makes the rules hard to enforce. On the other hand,
the availability of anonymous remailers makes untraceable violation of the
rules possible even without anonymous subscriptions. Someone intent upon
forwarding messages from this list to wherever can do so anonymously.
Anonymous posters could violate flaming rules, etc.

This could be reduced if unsigned anonymous postings were filtered. An
anonymous subscriber would have to supply a public key along with the
anonymous return address in order to post to the list. Then, unsigned
flames would get flushed, and signed flames would receive the usual
treatment.

Come to think of it, we could complain to the admin of the remailer used to
  repost list material illegally. Do you think that would satisfy people?

Eternal Optimist 

